%% Encryption on a Contoso file share - the four layers, who owns each key, and which legs are Contoso's to configure
%% Source: codex/blueprint-azure-files-secure-storage-account.md step 4 and codex/playbook-deploy-secure-storage-account-and-share.md step 4; Microsoft Learn - Enable infrastructure encryption for double encryption of data; Customer-managed keys for account encryption; SMB file shares in Azure Files (encryption in transit, Require Encryption in Transit for SMB, channel ciphers); Require secure transfer
flowchart TB
  subgraph MSFT["Microsoft owns and operates - no Contoso lever exists here"]
    SSE["Service-level SSE. 256-bit AES beneath the file system, FIPS 140-2 validated, ALWAYS on, cannot be disabled and does not need a client-side key to read the share"]
    INFRA["Infrastructure-level encryption. A SECOND 256-bit AES pass with a different algorithm and a separate Microsoft-managed key. Even under CMK this second key stays Microsoft-managed"]
    FABRIC["The private-endpoint fabric and the Microsoft backbone that carries the request from the endpoint NIC to the file service"]
    TERM["The SMB and TLS terminators inside the file service, which is where the negotiated cipher is actually enforced"]
  end

  subgraph ORG["Contoso owns - every one of these is a decision on the change record"]
    KEYSRC["encryption keySource. Microsoft.Storage is the baseline. Microsoft.Keyvault only if Contoso policy mandates CMK - assessor SEC-14 is informational either way"]
    DAY0["requireInfrastructureEncryption. CREATION TIME ONLY on a StorageV2 or premium account - it cannot be added to a live account and cannot be removed, so it is a day-0 decision, not a hardening step"]
    AKV["If CMK - the Key Vault or Managed HSM with soft delete AND purge protection on, an RSA or RSA-HSM key of 2048, 3072 or 4096 bits, and the user-assigned identity holding get, wrapKey and unwrapKey"]
    TLS["minimumTlsVersion TLS1_2 and supportsHttpsTrafficOnly true. Note the scope change - Secure transfer required now governs REST and HTTPS traffic ONLY"]
    EIT["Require Encryption in Transit for SMB. Portal-created accounts have it on. Accounts created by CLI, PowerShell or the FileREST API leave it Not selected, which is exactly how Contoso account was built"]
    CIPH["protocolSettings smb channelEncryption. Contoso baseline keeps AES-128-GCM and AES-256-GCM and drops AES-128-CCM, which caps the account at SMB 3.1.1 and SMB 3.0 clients that can do GCM"]
    KTIX["kerberosTicketEncryption AES-256, RC4-HMAC removed. This has to match Set-ADComputer KerberosEncryptionType AES256 on the contoso.local object or mounts fail with 1396"]
    FLEET["The client fleet itself. A Windows Server 2019 file server caps at AES-128-GCM, so selecting AES-256-GCM alone locks it out - the fleet, not Azure, sets the ceiling"]
    ER["The ExpressRoute private peering circuit and the Infoblox forwarder that keep the ciphertext off the internet in the first place"]
  end

  subgraph CONSULT["Consultant scope - the delivery team and the assessment kit"]
    RULES["The rule catalog that turns each setting above into a checkable finding, SEC-01 through SEC-15"]
    ORACLE["The oracle - re-export and re-assess, expect zero SEC and DATA findings other than SEC-04 shared key documented and SEC-14 platform-managed keys"]
    ORDER["The retrofit order - transport settings before SMB profile, SMB profile before keys, private path before the firewall"]
  end

  ATREST["Data at rest on the share - encrypted twice when infrastructure encryption was chosen at creation, once otherwise"]
  SMBLEG["Leg 1 - direct SMB mount, TCP 445 over ExpressRoute private peering to the file private endpoint. Confidentiality comes from SMB channel encryption, not TLS"]
  RESTLEG["Leg 2 - FileREST from the File Sync agent and from the portal browser, TCP 443, TLS 1.2 minimum"]
  MSLEG["Leg 3 - Storage Sync Service to the storage account and Azure Backup to the same account. Microsoft initiates it on the trusted-services path. It is encrypted, but Contoso cannot route it, inspect it or move it onto the circuit"]

  SSE --> ATREST
  INFRA --> ATREST
  KEYSRC -->|"wraps the account encryption key"| SSE
  AKV -->|"unwrap on every read and write"| SSE
  DAY0 --> INFRA
  TLS --> RESTLEG
  EIT --> SMBLEG
  CIPH --> SMBLEG
  KTIX --> SMBLEG
  FLEET -->|"sets the real ceiling"| CIPH
  ER --> SMBLEG
  ER --> RESTLEG
  SMBLEG --> TERM
  RESTLEG --> TERM
  TERM --> FABRIC
  FABRIC --> ATREST
  MSLEG -.->|"cannot be made private - state it in the report"| ATREST
  RULES --> ORACLE
  ORDER --> ORACLE
  ORACLE -.->|"evidence for the change record"| ORG
